{
  "comment": "The hook of the terminal (D-352, D-360). hooks: what one hook call becomes, at the time now (milliseconds); event null means the call changes nothing. The detail is one line of at most 40 characters, the last one an ellipsis when cut: the name of a file without its folder, the first line of a command, the host of a page, the tool part of a server tool. A permission notification is skipped: PermissionRequest tells it six seconds earlier, with the detail. files: the file of a session; an id that is not letters, digits and dashes, or longer than 64, has none. pulse: what a running session of Claude Code does, from its title (null, idle or working), its last event, and when the person last looked at it and typed into it. replaces: whether an event goes into the file over the one there. Async hooks run side by side, so a tool event after the end of a turn is a late one and is dropped; a message, a question or another end goes in. typed: whether input that went to the program was typed by the person; control sequences of the terminal itself (focus, cursor answers, arrows) are not, Enter, a digit and Esc are.",
